# clang-tidy checks for TrayMirror. Enabled checks are errors (spec 12.8:
# clang-tidy clean). The hook DLL is exempt (its target clears
# CXX_CLANG_TIDY): it is kernel32-only, allocation-free, exception-free
# code under deliberate C-style discipline (spec 12.4) that static
# analysis would fight rather than help; its gate is review + selftest.
# modernize-avoid-c-arrays is off for the same reason: proto wire structs
# and compile-time tables are plain C arrays by design so the same code
# can link into the STL-free hook DLL. readability-use-std-min-max is off
# because std::min would pull <algorithm> into hook-linked TUs.
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  readability-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -modernize-avoid-c-arrays,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-use-std-min-max
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
FormatStyle: file
